&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Salem, Ore.&lt;/strong&gt; &mdash; Some areas of Salem will see more flooding today. Waters will continue to rise until larger streams &ndash; Mill Creek, Shelton Ditch and lower Pringle Creek north of Mission Street &ndash; hit their peak sometime between 2 and 7 p.m. today.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;While significant rain is now over, the upper Mill Creek watershed received more rain overnight than anticipated. Flood water is now pushing through Salem. This flood water will impact areas of Mill Creek, Shelton Ditch and lower Pringle Creek north of Mission Street.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You can monitor stream conditions, traffic conditions and find sandbag locations through Salem&rsquo;s websites:&lt;/p&gt;

